<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<score-partwise version="4.0">
  <work><work-title>Engraving fixture: metre-based beat-grouping (R-2 B3/B4)</work-title></work>
  <identification>
    <creator type="arranger">Musicanyya test fixture</creator>
    <rights>CC0-1.0 (test fixture, original work)</rights>
    <encoding><software>Musicanyya</software><encoding-date>2026-09-23</encoding-date></encoding>
  </identification>
  <part-list>
    <score-part id="P1"><part-name>Piano</part-name></score-part>
  </part-list>
  <part id="P1">
  <!--
  Feature 006 fixture: one measure per metre, exercising beam rule R-2 B3 (groups-per-metre table) and
  B4 (4/4 / 2/2 / 3/4 eighth-note exceptions). No <beam> element is present anywhere in this file; every
  bar is filled EXACTLY (no rests, no tuplets, no dotted notes) so beat-grouping applies in its "plain"
  form. Pitches step through a diatonic (C major) scale so notes are individually addressable in test
  assertions. divisions=4 throughout, so eighth=2 division units, sixteenth=1 division unit.

  Expected beam-completion output, measure by measure:

  M1 (2/4) - four plain eighths C4 D4 E4 F4. Metre is x/4 -> one group per quarter (B3).
    Group 1 = beat 1 (C4, D4); Group 2 = beat 2 (E4, F4). Two 2-note primary (level-1) beams.

  M2 (3/4) - six plain eighths G4 A4 B4 C5 D5 E5. B4 3/4 exception: exactly six plain, non-tuplet eighths
    -> the WHOLE bar is one group (not per-quarter). One 6-note primary (level-1) beam, no secondary
    level (no note is shorter than an eighth).

  M3 (4/4) - beats 1-2: four plain eighths C4 D4 E4 F4 (exactly four plain eighths -> B4 4/4 exception:
    this half-bar is ONE group spanning both quarters). Beat 3: sixteenth G4, sixteenth A4, eighth B4.
    Beat 4: eighth C5, sixteenth D5, sixteenth E5. Because the second half-bar contains notes shorter
    than an eighth, it falls back to per-quarter grouping (B4), and grouping never crosses the bar's
    middle, so beat 3 and beat 4 are two SEPARATE groups (not joined to each other or to the first half).
    Level-1 (eighth) beams: Group A = C4-D4-E4-F4 (4-note beam, one continuous beam spanning the whole
    first half-bar). Group B = G4-A4-B4 (3-note beam). Group C = C5-D5-E5 (3-note beam).
    Level-2 (sixteenth) beams: within Group B, G4 and A4 are adjacent sixteenths -> a 2-note secondary
    beam G4-A4 (begin/end, no hooks needed since each has a same-level partner); B4 (eighth) carries no
    level-2 beam. Within Group C, D5 and E5 are adjacent sixteenths -> a 2-note secondary beam D5-E5
    (begin/end); C5 (eighth) carries no level-2 beam.

  M4 (2/2) - half-bar 1 (beats 1-2): four plain eighths F4 G4 A4 B4 with nothing shorter than an eighth
    -> stays as the base "one group per half note" (B3), i.e. ONE 4-note primary beam. Half-bar 2
    (beats 3-4) contains sixteenths -> B4 2/2 exception splits it into per-quarter groups: beat 3 =
    eighth C5, sixteenth D5, sixteenth E5 (3-note group); beat 4 = sixteenth F5, sixteenth G5, eighth A5
    (3-note group). Level-2 beams: D5-E5 (2-note secondary beam) in beat 3's group; F5-G5 (2-note
    secondary beam) in beat 4's group.

  M5 (3/8) - six plain sixteenths C5 D5 E5 F5 G5 A5, no eighth notes. x/8 with numerator <= 3 -> whole
    bar is one group (B3). Level-1 (eighth) beam: one continuous 6-note beam. Level-2 (sixteenth) beam:
    per B10, the secondary beam is NOT broken into two sub-groups of three - it stays ONE continuous
    6-note secondary beam across the whole bar, since all six notes sit inside the same single primary
    group.

  M6 (6/8) - six plain eighths C4 D4 E4 F4 G4 A4. Groups = one per dotted quarter (B3): Group 1 = C4 D4
    E4 (eighths 1-3); Group 2 = F4 G4 A4 (eighths 4-6). Two 3-note primary beams.

  M7 (9/8) - nine plain eighths C4 D4 E4 F4 G4 A4 B4 C5 D5. Groups = one per dotted quarter (B3): three
    groups of three eighths each: (C4 D4 E4), (F4 G4 A4), (B4 C5 D5).

  M8 (12/8) - twelve plain eighths C4 D4 E4 F4 G4 A4 B4 C5 D5 E5 F5 G5. Groups = one per dotted quarter
    (B3): four groups of three eighths each: (C4 D4 E4), (F4 G4 A4), (B4 C5 D5), (E5 F5 G5).

  M9 (5/8) - five plain eighths C4 D4 E4 F4 G4. B3: two groups, 3 eighths + 2 eighths. Group 1 = C4 D4 E4
    (3-note beam); Group 2 = F4 G4 (2-note beam).

  M10 (7/8) - seven plain eighths C4 D4 E4 F4 G4 A4 B4. B3: three groups, 2+2+3 eighths. Group 1 = C4 D4
    (2-note beam); Group 2 = E4 F4 (2-note beam); Group 3 = G4 A4 B4 (3-note beam).

  M11 (additive 3+2, <time><beats>3+2</beats><beat-type>8</beat-type></time>) - five plain eighths C4 D4
    E4 F4 G4. B3: groups follow the given sums in beat-type (eighth) units: Group 1 = first 3 eighths
    (C4 D4 E4); Group 2 = next 2 eighths (F4 G4).
  -->
  <measure number="1">
    <attributes>
      <divisions>4</divisions>
      <key><fifths>0</fifths></key>
      <time><beats>2</beats><beat-type>4</beat-type></time>
      <clef><sign>G</sign><line>2</line></clef>
